A lot of people in this thread have suggested running from ants.  This
can often not be an acceptable solution because they're fast, and thus
will get free hits sometimes as you flee from them.

As someone else has noted, soldier ants are the number one cause of
death in the game.  On alt.org's death list, there's 20% more death via
soldier ant than the next-leading cause (water moccasin).

They are dangerous for a fairly short period in a Nethack character's
life.  If a character gets to experience level 6 or 7, or finds a good
weapon or armor, he'll probably survive an encounter even with a small
group of them if fought one at a time.  The best way to handle soldier
ants, I would say, is to get strong enough fast enough that you can
kill them, or build your speed so you can run, or find out if they're
on the level early and avoid them that way (they don't follow off the
level if you take stairs or fall through a hole).

On getting strong quickly, the Gnomish Mines is usually a good source
of armor and weapons.  (Perhaps too good a source, really.)  Other than
that, and clever fleeing tactics, my best suggestion is to get a pet,
and get it buff.  Ants are low-level, so your pet will almost always
attack it.

